wrapping your entire app

501
00:34:32,350 --> 00:34:36,110
starting at your
layout.jsx file.

502
00:34:36,110 --> 00:34:39,230
Then you just need
to set up a slice.

503
00:34:39,230 --> 00:34:42,050
This is a super basic slice.

504
00:34:42,050 --> 00:34:47,590
It's less than 20 lines and
new line characters and all.

505
00:34:47,590 --> 00:34:52,870
When we set up our slices to
communicate with our Django

506
00:34:52,870 --> 00:34:55,730
store, this file will
get a bit bigger.

507
00:34:55,730 --> 00:35:03,040
It will also handle not only
updating our state data here

508
00:35:03,040 --> 00:35:08,800
in our front end
store, but we will also

509
00:35:08,800 --> 00:35:12,280
put in data to handle
network requests

510
00:35:12,280 --> 00:35:21,640
or get and post request
actions to our back end.

511
00:35:21,640 --> 00:35:24,680
And it will track those
asynchronously here

512
00:35:24,680 --> 00:35:26,180
in our slice.

513
00:35:26,180 --> 00:35:32,760
So this works really well for
just a super quick boilerplate

514
00:35:32,760 --> 00:35:36,160
state management for our app.

515
00:35:36,160 --> 00:35:37,640
And then when we
get to the point

516
00:35:37,640 --> 00:35:40,680
where we want to
add extra reducers,

517
00:35:40,680 --> 00:35:45,160
it also helps our network
request resolve asynchronously

518
00:35:45,160 --> 00:35:47,480
pretty easily, as well.

519
00:35:47,480 --> 00:35:51,960
If there are any questions,
go ahead and message me

520
00:35:51,960 --> 00:35:55,400
in Teams or in Canvas.

521
00:35:55,400 --> 00:35:56,500
Thanks.